Class
→ Blueprint for objects

Object
→ Instance of a class

Constructor
→ Initializes an object

Inheritance
→ Child gets properties/methods from parent

Polymorphism
→ One thing, many forms    (override, overloading)

Encapsulation
→ Hide data and control access    (private, public, protected, default)

Abstraction
→ Hide implementation, show essential details

Interface
→ Contract that a class implements

Overloading
→ Same method name, different parameters

Overriding
→ Child changes parent method implementation